cretary of  Homeland Security in as well to comment  out of the Coast Guard this is a  forecast track that the president held  up for  last week where it looked like the  hurricane was going to slam into the  Florida coast maybe even crossed the  potential and get into the Gulf of  Mexico you can see somebody with a  sharpie or some other writing instrument  added a little bit to the code of  uncertainty which was not part of the  official forecast which included the  Florida Panhandle in parts of Alabama  President Trump had tweeted over the  weekend that Alabama appeared to be in  the crosshairs and you could probably  extrapolate that if ahead of continued  on that track Alabama might have been  affected but it was never part of the  official forecast when asked this  afternoon how that marking got on the  map the president said he had no idea  right okay John Roberts live in the  North Lawn John thank you this is  hilarious but I really want to make an  effort to provide the right context for  these stories okay when it comes to this  Fox versus Trump thing let me zoom out a  little bit Fox News and even corporate  media more broadly are what we call  sense making tools and they are terrible  sense making tools for society so when  we talk about sense making and media  this is maybe one of the most important  analyses that we can do and I get it  we started with a sharpie but again I'm  making an effort to really provide  broader and important context through  when we do these media analyses stories  when we talk about the sense making  analysis for media it goes well beyond  the propaganda value of media we've  talked a lot about the propaganda value  of media and how media can sort of serve  corporate interests or political  interest for one party or another party  and you really have to zoom out to  understand this we are an estimated on  this planet we are an estimated seven  point seven billion people each kind of  existing in our little corner of it only  